        "content": "     1→[\n     2→  {\n     3→    \"title\": \"Qwen3.6-35B-A3B on my laptop drew me a better pelican than Claude Opus 4.7\",\n     4→    \"description\": \"Comparison between Alibaba's Qwen3.6-35B-A3B and Anthropic's Claude Opus 4.7 models using Simon's 'pelican riding a bicycle' benchmark. Local open source model is competitive with top-tier proprietary models.\",\n     5→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n     6→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n     7→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n     8→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-16\",\n     9→    \"topics\": [\"LLM\", \"benchmarks\", \"local-models\", \"qwen\", \"claude\", \"open-source\"],\n    10→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    11→  },\n    12→  {\n    13→    \"title\": \"llm-anthropic 0.25 Release\",\n    14→    \"description\": \"New model support for claude-opus-4.7 with thinking_effort:xhigh feature. New thinking_display and thinking_adaptive boolean options. Increased default max_tokens to maximum allowed for each model.\",\n    15→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    16→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    17→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    18→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-16\",\n    19→    \"topics\": [\"LLM\", \"anthropic\", \"claude\", \"tools\", \"api\"],\n    20→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    21→  },\n    22→  {\n    23→    \"title\": \"datasette 1.0a27 Release - CSRF Protection Changes\",\n    24→    \"description\": \"Datasette no longer uses Django-style CSRF form tokens, instead using modern browser headers (Sec-Fetch-Site) based on Filippo Valsorda's research. New RenameTableEvent for when tables are renamed during SQLite transactions.\",\n    25→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    26→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    27→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    28→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-15\",\n    29→    \"topics\": [\"security\", \"csrf\", \"datasette\", \"python\", \"sqlite\"],\n    30→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    31→  },\n    32→  {\n    33→    \"title\": \"Gemini 3.1 Flash TTS - Directed Text-to-Speech with Complex Prompting\",\n    34→    \"description\": \"Google released Gemini 3.1 Flash TTS, a text-to-speech model with surprisingly elaborate prompting capabilities requiring detailed character profiles, scene descriptions, and directorial notes. Simon vibe-coded a UI for trying it out.\",\n    35→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    36→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    37→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    38→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-15\",\n    39→    \"topics\": [\"google\", \"text-to-speech\", \"prompt-engineering\", \"tools\", \"gemini\", \"vibe-coding\"],\n    40→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    41→  },\n    42→  {\n    43→    \"title\": \"OpenAI Announces GPT-5.4-Cyber for Defensive Security\",\n    44→    \"description\": \"OpenAI released GPT-5.4-Cyber, a cyber-permissive model fine-tuned for defensive cybersecurity use cases. They also extended their 'Trusted Access for Cyber' program requiring identity verification via Persona.\",\n    45→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    46→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    47→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    48→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-14\",\n    49→    \"topics\": [\"security\", \"openai\", \"ai-security-research\", \"anthropic\"],\n    50→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    51→  },\n    52→  {\n    53→    \"title\": \"Cybersecurity Looks Like Proof of Work Now\",\n    54→    \"description\": \"UK's AI Safety Institute evaluation of Claude Mythos shows that more tokens (money) spent leads to better security results. This creates economic incentive to spend more on security reviews than attackers spend exploiting. Open source libraries become more valuable as security investment can be shared.\",\n    55→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison (citing Drew Breunig)\",\n    56→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    57→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    58→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-14\",\n    59→    \"topics\": [\"security\", \"ai\", \"open-source\", \"vibe-coding\", \"ai-security-research\"],\n    60→    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n    61→  },\n    62→  {\n    63→    \"title\": \"Servo v0.1.0 Crate - Embeddable Browser Engine for Rust\",\n    64→    \"description\": \"Simon used Claude Code to explore the new Servo crate, building a CLI tool called 'servo-shot' for taking screenshots. Servo provides an embeddable browser engine for Rust with clear API around ServoBuilder, WebView, and pixel readback methods.\",\n    65→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    66→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    67→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    68→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-13\",\n    69→    \"topics\": [\"browsers\", \"rust\", \"webassembly\", \"claude-code\", \"servo\"],\n    70→    \"type\": \"research\"\n    71→  },\n    72→  {\n    73→    \"title\": \"The Peril of Laziness Lost - LLMs Lack Virtue of Laziness\",\n    74→    \"description\": \"Bryan Cantrill argues that LLMs inherently lack the virtue of laziness - work costs nothing to them, so they create larger, not better systems. Human laziness forces us to develop crisp abstractions to avoid wasting our time.\",\n    75→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison (citing Bryan Cantrill)\",\n    76→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    77→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    78→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-13\",\n    79→    \"topics\": [\"ai\", \"llms\", \"ai-assisted-programming\", \"generative-ai\"],\n    80→    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n    81→  },\n    82→  {\n    83→    \"title\": \"Audio Transcription with Gemma 4 E2B using MLX\",\n    84→    \"description\": \"Simon shared a uv run recipe for transcribing audio files on macOS using the 10.28 GB Gemma 4 E2B model with MLX and mlx-vlm. Demonstrated successful transcription of a 14-second wav file with minor accuracy issues.\",\n    85→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    86→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    87→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    88→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-12\",\n    89→    \"topics\": [\"uv\", \"mlx\", \"ai\", \"gemma\", \"llms\", \"speech-to-text\", \"python\"],\n    90→    \"type\": \"tutorial\"\n    91→  },\n    92→  {\n    93→    \"title\": \"Google AI Edge Gallery - Official Gemma 4 iPhone App\",\n    94→    \"description\": \"Google released an official app for running Gemma 4 models (E2B and E4B sizes) directly on iPhone. The E2B model is a 2.54GB download, fast and useful. Includes image understanding, audio transcription, and interesting 'skills' demo with eight interactive widgets.\",\n    95→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    96→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    97→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    98→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-06\",\n    99→    \"topics\": [\"google\", \"iphone\", \"ai\", \"local-llms\", \"llms\", \"gemini\", \"llm-tool-use\"],\n   100→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   101→  },\n   102→  {\n   103→    \"title\": \"LLM Knowledge Bases - Andrej Karpathy's New Workflow\",\n   104→    \"description\": \"Karpathy shared a new workflow using LLMs to build personal knowledge bases for research topics. An 'LLM Wiki' pattern where AI agents compile living, evolving markdown libraries rather than traditional RAG retrieval. Works with tools like Obsidian for markdown-based knowledge management.\",\n   105→    \"author\": \"Andrej Karpathy\",\n   106→    \"source\": \"Twitter\",\n   107→    \"url\": \"https://x.com/karpathy/status/2039805659525644595\",\n   108→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-17\",\n   109→    \"topics\": [\"LLM\", \"knowledge-management\", \"workflow\", \"RAG\", \"obsidian\"],\n   110→    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n   111→  },\n   112→  {\n   113→    \"title\": \"Growing Gap in AI Understanding Based on Access Points\",\n   114→    \"description\": \"Andrej Karpathy notes the growing gap in understanding of AI capability based on access points and domains people use models with. OpenAI's free 'Advanced Voice Mode' runs on much older GPT-4o era model, while highest-tier Codex models can spend hours restructuring entire codebases.\",\n   115→    \"author\": \"Andrej Karpathy\",\n   116→    \"source\": \"Twitter\",\n   117→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n   118→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-10\",\n   119→    \"topics\": [\"openai\", \"chatgpt\", \"ai\", \"llms\", \"model-capabilities\"],\n   120→    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n   121→  },\n   122→  {\n   123→    \"title\": \"Anthropic launches Claude Design for Quick Visuals\",\n   124→    \"description\": \"Anthropic launched Claude Design, a new product for creating quick visuals. This is Anthropic's entry into the AI design space, competing with tools like Midjourney and DALL-E.\",\n   125→    \"author\": \"Aisha Malik\",\n   126→    \"source\": \"TechCrunch\",\n   127→    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/category/artificial-intelligence/\",\n   128→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-17\",\n   129→    \"topics\": [\"anthropic\", \"claude\", \"ai-design\", \"generative-ai\", \"tools\"],\n   130→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   131→  },\n   132→  {\n   133→    \"title\": \"'Tokenmaxxing' is Making Developers Less Productive\",\n   134→    \"description\": \"Tim Fernholz explores how 'tokenmaxxing' - the practice of maximizing LLM usage - may be making developers less productive than they think. The article questions whether excessive AI assistance is actually harming productivity.\",\n   135→    \"author\": \"Tim Fernholz\",\n   136→    \"source\": \"TechCrunch\",\n   137→    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/category/artificial-intelligence/\",\n   138→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-17\",\n   139→    \"topics\": [\"ai\", \"llms\", \"developer-productivity\", \"token-usage\", \"agentic-coding\"],\n   140→    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n   141→  },\n   142→  {\n   143→    \"title\": \"Cursor in Talks to Raise $2B+ at $50B Valuation\",\n   144→    \"description\": \"AI coding assistant Cursor is in talks to raise over $2B at a $50B valuation as enterprise growth surges. This reflects the massive growth and investment in AI-powered coding tools.\",\n   145→    \"author\": \"Marina Temkin\",\n   146→    \"source\": \"TechCrunch\",\n   147→    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/category/artificial-intelligence/\",\n   148→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-17\",\n   149→    \"topics\": [\"cursor\", \"ai-coding\", \"fundraising\", \"enterprise\", \"developer-tools\"],\n   150→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   151→  },\n   152→  {\n   153→    \"title\": \"Factory Hits $1.5B Valuation to Build AI Coding for Enterprises\",\n   154→    \"description\": \"Factory, an AI coding startup, reached $1.5B valuation to build AI coding tools for enterprises. This shows continued massive investment in AI-powered development tools.\",\n   155→    \"author\": \"Marina Temkin\",\n   156→    \"source\": \"TechCrunch\",\n   157→    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/category/artificial-intelligence/\",\n   158→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-16\",\n   159→    \"topics\": [\"ai-coding\", \"fundraising\", \"enterprise\", \"startups\", \"developer-tools\"],\n   160→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   161→  },\n   162→  {\n   163→    \"title\": \"OpenAI Takes Aim at Anthropic with Beefed-up Codex\",\n   164→    \"description\": \"OpenAI released an enhanced Codex model that gives it more power over your desktop, directly competing with Anthropic's Claude. This shows intensifying competition in AI coding assistance.\",\n   165→    \"author\": \"Lucas Ropek\",\n   166→    \"source\": \"TechCrunch\",\n   167→    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/category/artificial-intelligence/\",\n   168→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-16\",\n   169→    \"topics\": [\"openai\", \"codex\", \"anthropic\", \"ai-coding\", \"competition\"],\n   170→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   171→  },\n   172→  {\n   173→    \"title\": \"Show HN: Remoroo - Fixing Memory in Long-Running Coding Agents\",\n   174→    \"description\": \"Remoroo is a project showcased on Hacker News that attempts to fix memory issues in long-running coding agents. This highlights ongoing challenges with agent memory and context management.\",\n   175→    \"author\": \"adhamghazali\",\n   176→    \"source\": \"Hacker News\",\n   177→    \"url\": \"https://news.ycombinator.com/\",\n   178→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-19\",\n   179→    \"topics\": [\"agentic-coding\", \"memory\", \"hn\", \"developer-tools\"],\n   180→    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n   181→  },\n   182→  {\n   183→    \"title\": \"Graphs That Explain the State of AI in 2026\",\n   184→    \"description\": \"IEEE article with graphs explaining the state of AI in 2026, featured on Hacker News. Provides data-driven insights into AI developments and trends.\",\n   185→    \"author\": \"bryanrasmussen\",\n   186→    \"source\": \"Hacker News\",\n   187→    \"url\": \"https://news.ycombinator.com/\",\n   188→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-19\",\n   189→    \"topics\": [\"ai\", \"llms\", \"2026\", \"trends\", \"research\"],\n   190→    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n   191→  },\n   192→  {\n   193→    \"title\": \"Opus 4.7 to 4.6 Inflation is ~45%\",\n   194→    \"description\": \"Hacker News discussion about token inflation between Claude Opus 4.7 and 4.6 models, measuring approximately 45%. This highlights changing token economics in LLMs.\",\n   195→    \"author\": \"billchambers.me\",\n   196→    \"source\": \"Hacker News\",\n   197→    \"url\": \"https://news.ycombinator.com/\",\n   198→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-18\",\n   199→    \"topics\": [\"anthropic\", \"claude\", \"token-usage\", \"llms\", \"pricing\"],\n   200→    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n   201→  },\n   202→  {\n   203→    \"title\": \"Measuring Claude 4.7's Tokenizer Costs\",\n   204→    \"description\": \"Popular Hacker News post analyzing Claude 4.7's tokenizer costs with 677 points and 472 comments. Shows strong community interest in understanding LLM token economics.\",\n   205→    \"author\": \"aray07\",\n   206→    \"source\": \"Hacker News\",\n   207→    \"url\": \"https://news.ycombinator.com/\",\n   208→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-18\",\n   209→    \"topics\": [\"anthropic\", \"claude\", \"tokenization\", \"llms\", \"cost-analysis\"],\n   210→    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n   211→  },\n   212→  {\n   213→    \"title\": \"I'm Spending Months Coding the Old Way\",\n   214→    \"description\": \"Miguel Connor's Substack post featured on Hacker News about spending months coding without AI assistance. Generated 317 points and 305 comments, showing community debate about AI's role in coding.\",\n   215→    \"author\": \"miguelconner.substack.com\",\n   216→    \"source\": \"Hacker News\",\n   217→    \"url\": \"https://news.ycombinator.com/\",\n   218→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-18\",\n   219→    \"topics\": [\"ai-coding\", \"developer-experience\", \"workflow\", \"opinion\"],\n   220→    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n   221→  }\n   222→]\n   223→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
